hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"214","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Allah made Friday obligatory upon those before us, Allah guided us to it and they differed regarding it, so the people are behind us in this: the Jews (Saturday) and the Christians (Sunday)."""
"215","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is a moment on Friday such that if any Muslim is praying and asks Allah for any good during that moment, Allah grants it to him."""
"216","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""There is a moment on Friday in which if a Muslim person is praying and asks Allah for any good during it, Allah grants him that good, provided he does not ask for something sinful or for breaking family ties."""
"217","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever leaves three Jumu'ahs without a (legitimate) excuse, a seal is set upon his heart."""
"218","The daughter of Haritha bin Nu'man said: I saw that our oven and the oven of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) were the same. I learned Surah Qaf from the blessed mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) (by hearing it), he (peace be upon him) used to recite it on the pulpit on Fridays."
"219","Tawoos (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is obligatory upon every adult person to thoroughly clean himself for the sake of Allah once every seven days, even if he is not in a state of major impurity. On Friday, he should wash his head and his body."""
"220","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned the bath on Friday. Tawus (may Allah have mercy on him) stated: I said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): If he is with his family, should he apply perfume or oil? He replied: I do not know about that."
